# Project-local credentials for the Supabase MCP server.
#
# Copy this file to `.mcp.env` and paste your token there. `.mcp.env` is
# gitignored; this example file is not, and must never contain a real value.
#
# Read by scripts/supabase-mcp.mjs, which injects it into the MCP server
# process alone. Do NOT set this as a machine-wide environment variable
# (`setx` on Windows) — every process you run could then read it, including
# tooling for unrelated projects.
#
# ── Use a SCOPED token, not a classic one ────────────────────────────────
# Create it at https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens. A classic token
# carries your whole account: every organization and every project you belong
# to today, plus every one you create or join later. A scoped token carries
# only what you grant it.
#
# Scope it to the `connecta` project (ref szfkysqinjowmgdzonje) and grant:
#
#   Database          Read        list_tables, list_extensions, execute_sql,
#                                 generate_typescript_types
#   Migrations        Read        list_migrations
#   Migrations        Read-write  apply_migration  (only from Phase 1 onward)
#   Advisors          Read        get_advisors — the RLS/security linter
#   Project Settings  Read        get_project_url
#   API Keys          Read        get_publishable_keys
#   Storage           Read        list_storage_buckets
#   Logs              Read        query_logs
#
# Grant NOTHING under Organizations, Organization Projects, Organization
# Settings, or Projects (account-wide). Those are what make a token
# account-wide; without them this token cannot see that your other projects
# exist.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_your_scoped_token_here
